  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnerships for Decent Work in the Indo-Pacific Program (PDWIP) 2024/25 to 2027/28</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Partnerships for Decent Work in the Indo-Pacific Program (PDWIP) is a new program connecting Australia&apos;s aid program with trade unions in the Indo-Pacific.  The goal of the program is that &apos;The Indo-Pacific has decent work and sustained and inclusive economic growth&apos;.  The program will assist Australia in fulfilling its commitment to the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), specifically SDG 8 - Decent Work and seek to advance fair and decent work in the region.  The objective of PDWIP is &apos;Advancement of labour rights in the Indo-Pacific through collaboration and organisation.  End of Program Outcome (EOPO) is &apos;Participating unions act to advance workplace justice and support gender equality and climate justice through organising and campaigning by 2028&apos;.</narrative>
  </description>
